<v Aisha Begum>Sounds lovely compared with the broken coffee machine in the canteen. Started Monday with hot water that vaguely remembers a coffee bean.</v>

00:00:23.829 --> 00:00:25.929
<v Priya Raman>That's the premium setting, that is.</v>

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:34.719
<v Marcus Hale>Someone's got a new car in the car park, though. Very shiny. Parked miles from everyone else, naturally.</v>

00:00:37.189 --> 00:00:42.789
<v Callum Reid>Give it a week. It'll have the same coating of dust as the rest of ours.</v>

00:00:43.299 --> 00:00:47.500
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes the car park appreciation society. Finished bits first.</v>

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:54.850
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, so, finished the repair on the 11kV board last night. That's done, not another job for this shift.</v>

00:00:57.259 --> 00:01:01.460
<v Priya Raman>Right, you're talking about the repair that was on the previous list?</v>

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:04.170
<v Callum Reid>That's the one. Finished last night.</v>

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:12.310
<v Sarah Okafor>And I signed off the inspection on the IM1 on Tuesday. Last Tuesday, obviously. That's closed as well.</v>

00:01:13.159 --> 00:01:21.209
