00:05:34.970 --> 00:05:41.269
<v Sarah Okafor>Tomasz, could you also schedule downtime for the main isolation valve with production first thing tomorrow? Low priority.</v>

00:05:43.199 --> 00:05:48.800
<v Tomasz Nowak>I can't take that one, sorry. I'm not available for the production discussion first thing tomorrow.</v>

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:58.319
<v Sarah Okafor>All right. Grace Liu, can you take over scheduling downtime for the main isolation valve with production? First thing tomorrow, low priority.</v>

00:06:00.029 --> 00:06:08.430
<v Grace Liu>Yes, I'll take that instead of Tomasz. I'll schedule downtime for the main isolation valve with production first thing tomorrow. Low priority, got it.</v>

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:15.449
<v Callum Reid>Just separating the two things in my head: first thing tomorrow is the scheduling, not an agreed valve outage?</v>

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:21.610
<v Grace Liu>Correct, it's scheduling downtime with production. We're not agreeing an outage time in this call.</v>

00:06:22.139 --> 00:06:28.089
<v Priya Raman>Right. Always the bit that catches people out—when the admin happens versus when the kit actually stops.</v>

00:06:28.850 --> 00:06:36.199
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. And just to keep the urgency straight, the air dryer lock-out tag-out sign-off is the urgent one for today, Grace.</v>

00:06:38.129 --> 00:06:44.079
<v Grace Liu>Yep, that's clear. Air dryer sign-off today, urgent. The other two keep the timings we've just agreed.</v>

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:52.199
<v Tomasz Nowak>And I've got the new starters' training records Monday, whenever I get a chance, then the Palletiser guarding on Friday, top priority.</v>

00:06:53.860 --> 00:07:00.860
<v Marcus Hale>Mine are the boiler feed pump bearings Monday, fairly important, and the line 2 robot jam and sensors next Tuesday.</v>

00:07:02.689 --> 00:07:10.389
<v Aisha Begum>And no one's accidentally put me down to mend the coffee machine, have they? That was a complaint, not a heroic offer.</v>

00:07:12.129 --> 00:07:15.279
<v Sarah Okafor>Definitely a complaint. Very clearly minuted in spirit only.</v>

00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:18.500
<v Callum Reid>Lovely. All clear from production.</v>

00:07:20.050 --> 00:07:23.899
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, that's everything agreed. Thanks, all. See you in a bit.</v>
